<title>UK: Nynex volume boosted by b&amp;b trade.</title>
<headline>Nynex volume boosted by b&amp;b trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Share trading volume in Nynex Cable Comms Plc surged at the start of business on Friday in what traders said was a tax-related &quot;bed-and-breakfast&quot; trade.</p>
<p>The stock was up 1/2p at 114p by 0829 GMT, in volume of just under 28 million shares -- making it the most active stock in the London market.</p>
<p>In a bed and breakfast trade, an investor parks a poorly-performing stock with a broker overnight to realise a loss for tax purposes.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
